{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'allowlist|revocation|tag-lock|audit policy|policy gate|external repository|audit subject' /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/protocol/registry.md /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md | head -200\nnl -ba /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/protocol/core.md | sed -n '655,682p'\nnl -ba .task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md | sed -n '1336,1372p'\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/protocol/registry.md:62:### 2.1 Rotation and revocation\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/protocol/registry.md:109:source. Policy may forbid that through source allowlists.\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:16:allowlist, audit policy, and pinned registries. The configuration file SHOULD be\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:79:7. build the provider-first dependency closure, apply source allowlists and\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:83:8. run source-audit policy, resolve trusted registries and attestations, reject\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:84:   revocation or strict unknown results, and apply moved-tag policy; and\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:100:checks, audit, attestation, revocation, or moved-tag evaluation.\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:105:that it has tested against the `go-v1` conformance vectors. It MAY allowlist\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:180:unallowlisted toolchain is rejected rather than downloaded or approximated.\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:253:module, build, runtime, or audit cache; audit, registry, revocation, and\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:492:## 7. Source audit policy\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:505:- local hash or source revocation always blocks;\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1a52au/curator-spec-worktree/profiles/manager.md:513:not override local or registry revocation.\n   655\t- malformed commit/tag semantics use\n   656\t  `build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid`; and\n   657\t- a matched Git LFS pointer uses `build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported`.\n   658\t\n   659\tAfter raw-object proof, the manager MUST materialize exact blob bytes as one\n   660\timmutable regular-file snapshot. Before audit success, artifact-cache lookup,\n   661\tor a compiler child, it MUST validate the complete snapshot, compute\n   662\t`curator-build-source-v1`, parse the root descriptor, validate the selected\n   663\ttarget and module containment, and freeze that snapshot instance until the last\n   664\tbuild child exits.\n   665\t\n   666\tThe consuming skill and each effective external repository are independent\n   667\taudit subjects. The external audit subject MUST bind declared and effective\n   668\tidentity, object format, full effective commit, complete build-source digest,\n   669\tdescriptor target, substitution state, and successful exact-tag assertion when\n   670\tapplicable. Skill evidence MUST NOT attest an external repository; external\n   671\tevidence MUST NOT attest the skill. Audit-cache reuse requires exact subject\n   672\ttuple equality and MUST NOT bypass snapshot admission.\n   673\t\n   674\tThis ordering applies to real builds, claimed cache hits, and dry-runs that\n   675\tclaim source or audit coverage. A syntax-only offline operation that cannot\n   676\tobtain the exact snapshot MAY warn `build_repository_unverified_offline`, but\n   677\tMUST NOT claim source, audit, cache, receipt, marker, artifact, or installation\n   678\tcoverage. Install, update, repair, and coverage-claiming audit MUST fail\n   679\t`build_repository_source_unavailable` before mutation when the exact source\n   680\tcannot be obtained and audited.\n   681\t\n   682\t## 7. Closure resolution\n  1336\t## 7. Snapshot identity and audit equivalence\n  1337\t\n  1338\tThe consuming skill snapshot and each effective external repository snapshot are independent untrusted audit subjects.\n  1339\t\n  1340\tFor every external repository selected by the active plan:\n  1341\t\n  1342\t1. for an unsubstituted declaration containing `tag`, complete the exact-tag\n  1343\t   acquisition and terminal-lock equality check from section 6.3;\n  1344\t2. validate the whole repository snapshot;\n  1345\t3. compute `curator-build-source-v1` over every regular file, including `curator-build.json` and files outside the selected build root;\n  1346\t4. parse the descriptor and select the target;\n  1347\t5. audit the complete external snapshot under declared/effective identity, object format, effective commit, build-source digest, target, substitution state, and the verified tag assertion when applicable;\n  1348\t6. apply allowlist, revocation, registry, tag-lock, and audit policy gates;\n  1349\t7. only then inspect an artifact-cache candidate or start a compiler child.\n  1350\t\n  1351\tRegistry evidence for the skill does not attest the external repository. External evidence does not attest the skill. Audit cache reuse is allowed only when its subject tuple exactly matches the declared/effective state and snapshot digest; it does not bypass snapshot admission.\n  1352\t\n  1353\tA syntax-only offline check that cannot obtain an exact protected snapshot warns `build_repository_unverified_offline` and makes no source/audit/build claim. Install, update, repair, and coverage-claiming audit fail before mutation when the exact effective snapshot cannot be obtained and audited.\n  1354\t\n  1355\tDry-run may use network and removable operation-private fetch state, but it leaves no persistent repository, snapshot, audit response, lock, receipt, marker, or cache mutation. It must validate and audit the exact snapshot before reporting cache-hit or would-build.\n  1356\t\n  1357\t## 8. Receipt v2, cache identity, and mixed schema-7 builds\n  1358\t\n  1359\t### 8.1 Unsubstituted external receipt input\n  1360\t\n  1361\tReceipt-v2 input binds the complete source state:\n  1362\t\n  1363\t```json\n  1364\t{\n  1365\t  \"schema_version\": 2,\n  1366\t  \"driver\": \"go-repository-v1\",\n  1367\t  \"source\": {\n  1368\t    \"repository\": \"golden-tools\",\n  1369\t    \"declared\": {\n  1370\t      \"identity\": {\n  1371\t        \"kind\": \"network-git\",\n  1372\t        \"value\": \"github.com/example/golden-tools\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
